  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that the negation of a disjunction of two statements is equivalent to the conjunction of the negations of the individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(5\\text{ is integer}\\text{ or }5\\text{ is positive}) & ≡¬((5\\text{ is integer})∨(5\\text{ is positive})) \\\\  & ≡¬(5\\text{ is integer})∧¬(5\\text{ is positive}) \\\\  & ≡(5\\text{ is not integer})∧(5\\text{ is not positive}) \\\\  & ≡5\\text{ is not integer}\\text{ and }5\\text{ is not positive}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
